
                               TransEd Help
                               ------------


TransEd is TransAmiga's online text editor.  When entering text, do so
continuously, pressing RETURN only at the end of a paragraph.

TransEd has several control commands that you enter preceeded by a backslash
(\).  The backslash must be the very first command on a line in order for it
to be recognized.

Press \ by itself to take you to the edit menu where there are various
commands available for editting your message.

Press \q if your message is a reply to insert quoted lines from the original
message.  Quoted lines all have a '>' infront of them.  Use the B command
from the edit menu to view the contents of the quote buffer.

Commands within the editor can be "stacked", so, for example, you could enter
\s to save, or \ay to immediately abort the message.

